cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use XenoScan1 in your research, please cite this software and the associated publication when available."
title: "XenoScan1: alignment-free discovery of horizontal gene transfer through reference-relative genomic discordance"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Boctor
    given-names: Joseph
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4103-1594"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JosephBoctor/XenoScanHGT"
url: "https://github.com/JosephBoctor/XenoScanHGT/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - horizontal gene transfer
  - HGT
  - comparative genomics
  - bioinformatics
  - machine learning
  - alignment-free sequence analysis
  - genomic composition
abstract: >-
  XenoScan1 is a machine-learning framework for identifying candidate
  horizontal gene transfer sequences through reference-relative genomic
  discordance. It projects query DNA sequences into a host-relative feature
  space using a precomputed universal reference manifold and applies a
  pre-trained Random Forest model to estimate HGT-associated scores.
  Predictions are computational evidence for candidate sequences and do not,
  by themselves, establish that horizontal transfer has occurred.
